HTML structure & semantics
•	lang="eng" → lang="en" on every page (a real, standard language code)
•	Removed the deprecated <center> and <u> tags and the uppercase <H1> — replaced with proper <h1>/<h2> and CSS for centering/underlining
•	Fixed heading misuse: your <h3> tags were being used for body paragraphs and even wrapped around a <ul>'s <li> items on the Service page .Content is now in <p> tags, with real <h2> section headings
What was removed
•	All inline style="..." attributes (image sizing, the pink background-color: rgb(255,192,203) on every page) — moved into the shared stylesheet
•	The literal "|" characters typed into the nav link text (HOME|, ABOUT|, etc.) — separation is now done with CSS
•	The "Please find the following as a navigation..." helper sentence — no longer needed since the nav is a real navigation bar at the top, not buried at the bottom of the page
•	The empty, non-functional <a href="PDF FILE"></a> on the gallery page
•	The odd "5L 10L and 20L" sizing text on the gallery page (didn't fit baked goods — flagged for you to clarify)
•	The duplicate gallery page paste (you sent it twice, identical)
Accessibility
•	Every <img> now has descriptive alt text (originally none did)
•	The hamburger menu button and back-to-top button have aria-labels
•	The mobile nav toggle has aria-expanded so screen readers know if it's open
CSS / visual design
•	Built css/stylesheet.css from scratch — none of your pages linked a stylesheet except home.html, and even that had no actual styling written yet
•	Cream/brown/gold color palette (replacing the pink background) with CSS variables so colors are consistent and easy to change later
•	Responsive layout: flexbox/grid that reflows for tablet and phone screens, using @media queries
•	Hover/zoom effects on gallery images and nav links, card-style shadows and rounded corners on content sections
JavaScript (js/script.js) — the interactive layer
•	Mobile hamburger menu: nav collapses into a toggle button on small screens
•	Active-page highlighting: automatically detects which page you're on and highlights it in the nav — no manual class needed per page
•	Back-to-top button: fades in after scrolling, smooth-scrolls up on click
•	Lightbox (gallery page only): click any photo to see it enlarged; close with the ✕, clicking outside it, or Esc
Page-specific content fixes
•	Home: fixed the broken <video><source src="images/"> (empty, no file) → now points to videos/bakery-process.mp4 with a type attribute and fallback text; removed a repeated phrase in the intro paragraph
•	About: "Ms.Monotwe" → "Ms. Monotwe", "Queens Cakes" → "queen cakes"
•	Contact: phone and email are now clickable tel:/mailto: links instead of plain text
•	Service: the invalid <h3>-wrapped list fixed into a proper <ul>, each item styled with a checkmark
Everything not mentioned (your actual page copy, business info, image files) was left untouched.
